# Opt in held owner and decode leaf observations

This model-only stage narrows two opaque coordinator spans identified by the
[offline capture attribution](../../docs/testing/performance/0.74/capture-attribution-result-20261026.md).
It does not split `Child::wait_with_output`: the current Rust helper exposes no
separate wait versus pipe-collection boundary without replacing its mechanism.
The worker helper and CI Job-list creation implementation remain byte-identical.
No native control, V6, product workload or server/service/clock action occurs.

The exact additional flags `--coordinator-frames --capture-leaves` select a
separate exclusive output root. Old default and outer-only modes retain their
measure functions, result shapes and clock budgets. Intent precedes lazy leaf
import/schema checks and all original preflights. Both arms keep the same worker,
sixteen-worker schedule, ordinary Git calls, shared 120-second origin, five-second
cleanup, pins, disk/log bounds, terminal checks and estimator. No renewal occurs.

Two owner leaves surround original identity/path checks and initial held-process
read/validation. The specialized setter publishes `_child` before its first
probe; the original API's finally and owned cleanup retain that child on failure.
No clock observation is inserted between successful CreateProcessW and child
publication, before error consumption, or inside setup/cleanup. The original CI
API and Win32 last-error path are not wrapped. Owner leaves are part of spawn,
not pure native creation cost; setup, publication and resume remain unseparated.

Six decode leaves surround log stat/bound, log read, text decode, JSON record
parse, original protocol validation and result join/residual checks. The
unchanged compound `rows(log_path.read_bytes(), ...)` is replaced only by the
leaf-aware rows equivalent with an extra recorder argument. Log-read timing ends
at that function's entry, after argument evaluation. It includes the read and
call boundary, not pure disk IO. All original rows operations and predicates
retain their AST and order. No manual pipe drain or concurrent reader is added.

The [protocol](capture-leaves-protocol.toml) fixes four owner probes and twelve
decode probes: at most sixteen additional probes/48 clock reads per worker,
84 including the unchanged outer recorder. Raw bracket domains and zero values
remain. CPU is process-wide coordinator CPU, not worker or native Git phase CPU;
wall bounds concern bracketed CPU-read instants, not effect-only cost. Leaves
are nested inside outer spans and must not be added to them.
Recorder construction/export and sample-file append are not a complete part of
the original frame metric; their elapsed time still consumes the shared cohort
deadline. Zero deltas do not certify absent work or timer precision.

The first ordinary leaf fault freezes both leaf groups without retry or fallback
clock. Original owner execution/wait/close continues. The independent outer Tape
keeps its prior policy; neither recorder rewrites the original operational
verdict or cleanup errors. Outer refusal is retained if already present when
leaf attachment is finalized; this is deterministic metadata precedence, not a
claim of cross-recorder temporal error order. Incomplete/raw partial spans have
no invented endpoints; later spans are not observed, not claimed unexecuted.
Fatal interrupts use the original exception/finally custody path.

Restricted AST comparison strips only literal leaf marks and the final leaf
attachment, normalizes the exact job/rows substitutions, and compares the owner
setter and rows body separately. Differential models preserve original calls,
argv, four deadline reads, metric fields, first refusals and healthy close.
Every additional clock-read position is tested for ordinary and fatal failure.
The first short-temp-path fixture refusal is retained; expected paths are
canonicalized only in the corrected fixture, not in the product predicate.

Native clock/process compatibility and cost of enabled leaves remain unproven.
A later native control requires its own exact source/build and first-result
retention. Recorder overhead still requires a separate on/off design. No leaf
result may relax a live predicate, deadline, full-package or production gate.
